{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"636012145204527127","content":"so either I really am good, and all that is true.... or I really am evil beyond measure, and playing a very very well played manipulative game.  Or possibly at any given point, the good part of me is hairs breadth away from breaking, and he might go evil.  In D&D people think of good and evil as literal good and evil.  But if you really get into what alignment means... good is selflessness.... evil is selfishness.  Law is having  code, an ethic, a morality, and not breaking it no matter what.... chaos is constantly breaking what you believe, testing your limits, to be reformed into something new.","created_at":"2020-08-12T15:21:37.373000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"743127058472763445","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
